{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Statutory right for employees to take paid leave for religious festivals",
        "additional_details": "No one should have to choose between their job and practising their faith. We ask the Government to provide a statutory right to leave for religious festivals, without employees having to sacrifice their annual holiday allowance. Reasonable notice and arrangements could help employers manage staffing needs. We believe everyone should have the right to observe their faith.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to introduce a statutory right for employees to take paid or unpaid leave for religious festivals in addition to their annual leave allowance. Many employees are refused time off to celebrate important religious occasions with their families. ",
